This is a testing file for an API server to stream EMG data on an OpenBCI Ganglion

To use:
*if you have any problems with these steps check the Detailed Documentation file*
- BEFORE ANYTHING: ensure your RPi has been setup as an access point
- install requirements: pip install -r requirements.txt
- create a config.json file in config/ that follows the same structure as config.json.example
- change the <IPv4> address to the one associated with your device
    - or for local connections keep as "0.0.0.0"
- in your terminal run: python main.py 

Note: This code is adapted for Linux OS/RaspberryPi, in order to use on Windows:
- winget install --interactive usbipd-win (install usbipd tool; in PowerShell as Admin)
- usbipd wsl list (look for OpenBCI dongle -> get BUSID)
- usbipd wsl attach --busid <your-bus-id> (attach dongle to WSL)
- ls /dev/tty* (check if device is visible on Ubuntu (WSL) terminal)
    - the name will either be /dev/ttyACM0 or /dev/ttyUSB0
- sudo adduser $USER dialout (give permission to access serial port (reopen Ubuntu terminal))

Overall Architecture:
[ OpenBCI Ganglion ]
       |
       v
[ Python Server (main.py) ]  <-- Catches the raw data
       |
       +-------------------------------------------+
       |                                           |
  [ Path 1: Visualization (index.html)]      (Path 2: Data Processing)
       |                                        |                 |
  [ WebSockets ]                         [ LSL Outlet ]   [ CSV Files ]
       |                                        |                 |
       v                                        v                 v
  [ Browser ]                                    [ Local Network ] 
(You see live EMG data)              

Data Processing Architecture:
                     

Data Threads:
    1. Main asynchronous thread (FastAPI/Uvicorn): central engine of app instance, controlled by asyncio Event Loop (non-blocking)
    2. EMG worker thread: handles hardware interaction and data processing, thread=ganglion_instance._emg_thread (blocking)